  "verdict": "INDETERMINATE \u2014 NOT durable. 58/118 soft esports picks have a realizable entry (49.2%); the realizable ROI-turn LB is 0.116 over 40 match-clusters BUT: INDETERMINATE (LODO-drop-dota2-kills-edge). The apparent edge is a short-window, single-discipline favorite-chalk artifact (disciplines={'lol': 9, 'dota2': 20, 'cs2': 9, 'val': 2}, active_days=7, LODO-drop-dota2 LB=-0.102) \u2014 the 'fat edge on a soft week' trap the run is built to reject. The conversion gap IS closed (soft_fav captures real esports consensus the rank-40 gate misses), but whether the softer market yields a fatter, more-CONSISTENT per-dollar edge than the crowded favorites is NOT answerable at realizable cost on this data: the arm never ran live, so ask coverage is thin and the clob tape is only 72h \u2014 there is no multi-regime realizable history to validate durability. The pre-registered forward gate is the arbiter. Directional ceiling (NOT copyable) + belief-blind skill are context only; a directional/soft-week number is exactly what must NOT be reported as an edge."
